+### 5.9 conversation_list
+
+Delivers the authenticated user's conversation summaries in response to a `list_conversations` frame. Absent when `transport.history` is not enabled. No `stream_end` follows this frame.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "conversation_list",
+  "conversations": [
+    {
+      "sessionId": "s1",
+      "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
+      "updatedAt": "2026-11-07T12:00:00.000Z",
+      "entryCount": 4
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field           | Type                  | Description                                       |
+| --------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | string                | `"conversation_list"`                             |
+| `conversations` | ConversationSummary[] | Newest-first summaries for the authenticated user |
+
+`ConversationSummary`: `sessionId` (string), `createdAt` (ISO 8601 string), `updatedAt` (ISO 8601 string), `entryCount` (number).
+
+- With `transport.history.enabled`, the server answers a `list_conversations` frame with a `conversation_list` whose summaries carry ISO 8601 strings for `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, no `stream_end` follows, and the user id is taken from the connection's authenticated user — a `userId` field in the frame is ignored ([validated by: answers conversation_list from ws.userId with ISO-string dates and no stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L102)).
+- Without `transport.history.enabled`, or when the store implements no `listFor`, the server answers with an `error` frame whose code is `UNSUPPORTED`; when `listFor` rejects, the code is `SERVER_ERROR` ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when history is off or the store lacks listFor, SERVER_ERROR when listFor rejects](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+- The server answers `list_conversations` off the per-session lock, so it arrives before the `stream_end` of any `user_message` turn running concurrently on the same session ([validated by: answers list_conversations before the user_message stream_end of a concurrent turn](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L156)).
+
